# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The context is the repository root (`context: .` in docker-compose.yml), not
# src/ — the Dockerfile COPYs .docker/, scripts/, recipes/ and drush/, which live
# outside it. Narrowing the context to src/ would not remove the need for this
# file either: every expensive and every sensitive path below is INSIDE src/,
# because src/ is simultaneously your committed source, Composer's install
# target, and Drupal's runtime state directory. See docs/image-build.md.
#
# This is a DENYLIST, deliberately. An allowlist (`*` then re-include) fails by
# omitting a directory nobody remembered to add — silently, as a cache hit, and
# only in production, because local dev bind-mounts ./src and works regardless.
# A denylist fails by shipping something extra, which is a size cost rather than
# an outage. docs/image-build.md has the measurements.
#
# The list is not the control — `ahoy image-manifest` is. It builds the image and
# diffs its contents against .docker/image-manifest.txt, so both directions get
# caught: crap arriving, and directories vanishing. Run it after changing this
# file or adding a top-level directory under src/.
#
# Local development is unaffected by everything here: docker-compose.override.yml
# bind-mounts ./src over /opt/drupal, so the container sees the host tree no
# matter what the image contains. That is also why a mistake here is invisible
# until deploy.

# ── Repository and tooling metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
.circleci
.claude
.claude-scratchpad
.serena
.logs
docs
.visual-regression
*.md

# ── Local environment, data and state ────────────────────────────────────────
.data
.env
docker-compose.local.yml
# Drupal's runtime state. Uploads can be gigabytes, and in a deployed
# environment this path is a mounted volume, not image content.
src/web/sites/default/files
# Per-developer overrides. settings.php includes settings.local.php LAST, so a
# copy baked into the image would win over the platform's environment.
src/web/sites/default/settings.local.php
src/web/sites/default/services.local.yml

# ── Front-end ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never needed at runtime, and the largest thing in the context.
**/node_modules

# ── Composer-managed trees, rebuilt inside the image with --no-dev ───────────
#
# THE RULE: this block mirrors `extra.installer-paths` in src/composer.json,
# minus the two custom/ targets you own. Add a line here whenever you add an
# installer path. It has drifted before — drush/Commands/contrib was missing,
# so a Composer-installed drush package shipped as a duplicate of the one the
# image's own install had already placed.
#
# Without these, `COPY src/ /opt/drupal/` lays the host tree over the image's
# `composer install --no-dev` from several layers earlier — and after a local
# `ahoy build` that host tree holds every dev dependency, so the production
# image ships PHPUnit, PHPStan, Behat, Rector and drupal/coder.
src/vendor
src/bin
src/web/core
src/web/libraries
src/web/modules/contrib
src/web/profiles/contrib
# Contrib themes are Composer-managed, except CivicTheme — the committed
# product this monorepo develops — which must ship in the image.
src/web/themes/contrib/*
!src/web/themes/contrib/civictheme
# Theme build inputs/outputs that never ship: node deps (also matched by
# **/node_modules), Storybook output (CI-built, deployed to Netlify — never in
# the image), and the uikit-installed components/ + dist/, which the assets
# stage rebuilds and overlays — excluding them keeps a stale local build out
# of the context and the layer cache honest.
src/web/themes/contrib/civictheme/storybook-static
src/web/themes/contrib/civictheme/components
src/web/themes/contrib/civictheme/dist
src/drush/Commands/contrib
src/recipes/contrib

# ── GovCMS variant manifests — CI/local only, the deployed image is d11-only ─
src/composer.govcms.json
src/composer.govcms.lock

# ── drupal-scaffold artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Written into src/ by `composer drupal:scaffold` (see the same entries in
# .gitignore). They exist only on a machine that has run `ahoy build`, never in
# a clean CI checkout — so excluding them keeps the context identical in both
# places, which is what makes `ahoy image-manifest` comparable between them.
# None has a runtime role.
src/.editorconfig
src/.gitattributes
src/recipes/README.txt

# ── Test and QA material ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The image is built with COMPOSER_NO_DEV=true, so it has no phpunit, behat,
# phpcs, phpstan, phpmd or rector binary and cannot run any of this. Locally
# these all run against the ./src bind mount, and CI lint runs on the host
# checkout — neither reads the image copy, so excluding them changes nothing
# except what a production image carries.
#
# src/shipshape.yml is NOT here: `ahoy ship-shape` runs the shipshape binary,
# which IS baked into the image, against /opt/drupal/shipshape.yml.
src/tests
src/behat.yml
src/phpcs.xml
src/phpmd.xml
src/phpstan.neon
src/phpstan-govcms.neon
src/phpunit.xml
src/rector.php
src/.twig-cs-fixer.php

# ── Generated sub-theme ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# civictheme_demo is generated at build (image) or provision (local) time and
# never committed. The Dockerfile's subtheme + assets stages produce and build
# it, and `COPY --from=assets` overlays it after `COPY src/` — a stale local
# copy in the context would only pollute the layer cache, since COPY merges
# directories rather than replacing them.
src/web/themes/custom/civictheme_demo
src/web/themes/contrib/civictheme_demo
